  "summary": "Today's health-tech landscape shows significant movement on multiple fronts. Drug discovery and delivery are advancing with Novo Nordisk partnering with Anthropic on AI-powered development while Novartis acquires Sironax's blood-brain barrier technology for $125 million to address pipeline challenges. Several funding rounds underscore investor confidence in specialized platforms, including Evvy's $40 million for vaginal microbiome analysis and Thatch's $108 million raise at unicorn valuation. On the policy side, political shifts are reshaping healthcare economics—GOP efforts aim to make Medicare Advantage mathematics more favorable to insurers while simultaneously hospitals are dropping MA plans due to rising denial rates and steering patients back to traditional Medicare. AI integration in clinical settings is progressing thoughtfully, with physicians emphasizing that AI works best when seamlessly embedded in workflows rather than taking over decisions, while CMS expands the ACCESS Model to cover additional chronic conditions. Meanwhile, emerging concerns include teenage reliance on AI chatbots as mental health substitutes and ongoing scrutiny of drug-pricing initiatives under the Trump administration.",
